In this strategy, companies work at improving high-quality products capable of lasting a lifetime. In every industrial sector, it is possible to find long-lasting products, confirming the fact that this strategy is economically profitable. The high added value of products will strengthen customer loyalty and the positive image of the brand. This strategy can be mixed with the design for leasing or sharing of the product in order to maintain the investment for longer profit gains.  However, the designer should take into account that some technologies get obsolete quickly even if the product is still working perfectly. In this case, perhaps, an upgrade program can incentivize users to spend more money on premium products.